              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for to be startled, then the Hindi for astonished."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: धमाका",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "धमाका — dhamākā — \"a bang; a blast\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "रात को एक ज़ोर का धमाका हुआ। rāt ko ek zor kā dhamākā huā. There was a loud bang in the night."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "धमाका (dhamākā) is probably imitative, built on dham, the sound of a heavy thud. CDIAL reconstructs dhamm, \"noise\" (CDIAL 6735), and lists Hindi dhamādham, noisily, under it, though not this word itself. धमाका होना is for there to be a bang."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
